------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Once.Format.Proof.Counts — the printer counts the anchors it writes
-- (plan 0.124 step 4.5).
--
-- Every printer advances the anchor index by a count of its own, whatever
-- the trivia, and writes exactly that many anchor tokens (`Ind`): an anchor
-- is one, a token that is not one none. So a declaration's anchors, as the
-- printer numbers them, are the anchor tokens of its printed text. And
-- its comments' words are its anchors' notes', in order (`cms`): each
-- anchor's comments before it, then those at the end of its line.
--
-- Generated by `scripts/gen-format-counts.py` (the printer induction is the
-- one `Proof.Canon` uses, `scripts/format_printers.py`): edit the generator,
-- not this file.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

